// Where a piece of ground is, in a form a country can be named after.
//
// Every entry may declare any of three ways to be recognised, strongest first:
//   "regions":  exact region ids from common/states;
//   "names":    region names as common/states spells them, with "countries" to narrow it;
//   "bbox":     [latMin, latMax, lonMin, lonMax] around the leaving ground.
//
// "macro": true marks a whole side of a continent. A macro land only names a state when it
// holds most of the ground leaving (60%), so a single restive province cannot borrow the
// name of Siberia or the Balkans. A narrow land needs half.
